---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { installUrl, route } from '../lib/release';
---

<Page title="Setup guide">
  <article class="reading shell">
    <h1>Setup guide</h1>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Install <a href="https://violentmonkey.github.io/get-it/"
          >Violentmonkey</a
        >, or a compatible userscript manager.
      </li><li>
        Open the <a href={installUrl}>Tempo Control userscript</a> and confirm Install.
        If you see source code instead, use your manager’s “Install from URL” option
        on the published site, or paste the script into a new script for local testing.
      </li><li>
        Reload SoundCloud and choose a track. Use the tempo controls in the
        bottom player.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <section>
      <h2>Find your speed</h2><p>
        The slider goes from 0.025× to 2× in 0.025× steps. Type an exact value
        for up to 4×. Double-click the number or slider to reset to 1×;
        Shift-click the arrows for 0.01× adjustments.
      </p><p>
        Use the bookmark button to remember a track’s speed. The gear opens
        settings, saved tracks and the tempo editor.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="sharing">
      <h2>Send your version</h2><p>
        Open the tempo editor and choose Copy link. It includes the track, tempo
        points, fades and pitch mode. Your friend needs Tempo Control installed
        to preview and apply it.
      </p><p>
        For everyday sharing, enable “Include tempo in copied links” in
        settings. Then copying the current, loaded track’s full SoundCloud link
        can include your adjustments. Unloaded tracks and short links may stay
        unchanged.
      </p><p>
        Without the script, the link still opens the normal SoundCloud track.
        Opening a tempo link does not automatically play audio or overwrite
        saved settings.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="limits">
      <h2>Pitch modes</h2><p>
        Natural mode changes pitch with speed. Preserve key keeps the original
        key using Signalsmith when the player’s audio routing is available, with
        browser correction as a fallback at 0.25× or higher. Lower speeds use
        buffered audio and require a supported stream. Preserve key below 0.25×
        requires WASM.
      </p><p>
        Time-stretching can introduce artifacts, especially at extreme speeds.
        Processing adds some latency. The Output level setting applies to both
        pitch modes across SoundCloud.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Where things are stored</h2><p>
        Settings and saved timelines stay in SoundCloud’s local site storage in
        this browser. Export a backup from settings before clearing browser
        data.
      </p><a href={route('privacy/')}>Privacy details</a>
    </section>
    <section id="troubleshooting">
      <h2>If something isn’t working</h2>
      <p>
        Missing controls? Check that Tempo Control is enabled in your userscript
        manager, then reload SoundCloud. Disable older copies of the script.
      </p>
      <p>
        For audio problems, switch off WASM in settings and try Browser
        processing. If a website preview fails to load, choose Retry, load an
        audio file or use the synth sample.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
